          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a car model humidifier?",
            "answer": "<p>It is a detailed car model with a small ultrasonic humidifier inside. Fill it with water, plug it into USB and cool mist flows from the exhausts while the lights glow – a humidifier, aroma diffuser and display piece in one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does it work?",
            "answer": "<p>Open the water tank, fill it with clean tap water, add a few drops of car-safe diffuser oil if you like, and plug it into any USB port. Press the button once and cool mist rolls out of the exhausts while the headlights and tail-lights glow.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is it powered?",
            "answer": "<p>Every DriveMist humidifier runs on 5 V USB power, so it works from the USB port in your car, a laptop, a power bank or a standard phone charger. The cable is included in the box.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use essential oils or car fragrance?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Add 2–3 drops of water-soluble essential oil or car diffuser fragrance to the water tank and it doubles as an aroma diffuser and car air freshener. Avoid thick or oil-only perfumes, which can clog the atomiser.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it safe to use in the car?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. It runs on low-voltage USB power and switches itself off automatically when the tank runs dry, so it never runs empty. Place it in a cup holder or on a flat, non-slip surface, never where it could block your view or an airbag, and refill it only while parked.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it make my car or dashboard wet?",
            "answer": "<p>No. The mist is very fine and evaporates quickly. Keep it upright, don’t overfill the tank, and point the exhausts away from screens and electronics.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does one tank last?",
            "answer": "<p>It depends on the model and the mist mode, but a full tank typically lasts a commute or a long evening. Check the product page for each model’s details.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean it?",
            "answer": "<p>Empty the tank after use, wipe it dry and clean the atomiser once a week with a cotton bud and a little white vinegar. That keeps the mist strong and the water fresh.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use it at home or in the office?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Plenty of customers keep theirs on a desk, bedside table or gaming setup as a night light, mini humidifier and display model in one.</p>"
          }
        },
